Split screen (2 Players) drawing, two changes in the vertex pulling path:

1. The per-frame index buffer of indexed vertex-pulled draws holds 1<<22 indices (was 1<<21; 16 MB more upload memory).
   A J-Stars 2 Players frame needs about 1.6M indices, so with 1<<21 every split screen frame was cut in two batches
   with a GPU wait between them ([MIDFLUSH] on every frame). The [MIDFLUSH] line now says which buffer was full.
2. Gathered copies (VPULL_GATHER, default on; VPULL_GATHER=0 turns it off): a batch the sparse check would send to the
   CPU path (it uses a few vertices of a big mesh, as each split screen view does) copies only the vertices it uses,
   one after the other, and its indices count them from 0, as a record of its own. Up to 1<<20 vertices (tables of
   12 MB, allocated on first use); the common strides are copied with fixed-size copies. The [VPULL] report counts
   them as "gathered".

J-Stars, 2 Players 2 vs 2 on Hidden Leaf, median frame rate: 18-24 before, 28-30 after with two-thread drawing
(PIPE=1); pulled draws 81% -> 100%. 1 Player is unchanged (30.0). Pictures checked in the test runs' shots.
